{"archetypes":[{"name":"cli-envelope","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"Claude subprocess launchers now depend on JSON output envelopes while downstream collectors still expect prose and stable failure behavior.","prompt_body":"Investigate the changes around spawned Claude CLI invocations, especially whether --output-format json is composed safely with existing flags and whether .result extraction preserves collector-facing output. Check exit status handling, stderr handling, malformed JSON behavior, and whether token usage recording can fail without masking the subprocess result. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"cost-pipeline","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"A fourth token lane must be consistently priced, aggregated, rendered, and analyzed across shell and Python paths.","prompt_body":"Trace the claude_sub lane end to end through token-report assembly, token-cost pricing, render-cost-line, render-run-summary, final-summary writers, and the Python report-tokens modules. Look for mismatched flag names, missing totals, wrong Claude-rate reuse, inconsistent bucket fallback behavior, or places where total cost/tokens omit the new lane. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"schema-compat","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The change expands persisted token-report and run-summary schemas consumed by committed logs, fixtures, and downstream parsers.","prompt_body":"Review the persisted data-shape changes for token-report JSON, BUCKETS_claude_sub, vendor arrays, cost-line text, golden fixtures, and run-log documentation. Focus on backward compatibility with reports lacking claude_sub, deterministic lane ordering, avoiding collision with the transcript-derived claude key, and consistency of display label versus machine name. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
